// Title: Renamed Jusched.EXE Execution
// Sigma ID: edd8a48c-1b9f-4ba1-83aa-490338cd1ccb
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Markus Neis, Swisscom
// Date: 2019-06-04 | Modified: 2023-02-03
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1036.003
// Description: Detects the execution of a renamed "jusched.exe" as seen used by the cobalt group
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.bitdefender.com/files/News/CaseStudies/study/262/Bitdefender-WhitePaper-An-APT-Blueprint-Gaining-New-Visibility-into-Financial-Threats-interactive.pdf
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/adf5a626c4a776f3f023056f0f398b9523a2f09e/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_renamed_jusched.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessVersionInfoFileDescription in~ ("Java Update Scheduler", "Java(TM) Update Scheduler")) and (not(FolderPath endswith "\\jusched.exe"))
